            <ArticleTitle>[Four first Congolese cases of pelvic ankylosing spondylitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>21-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report four ankylosing spondylitis cases observed within 11 years (1990-2000) of rheumatologic exercise among 10,000 patients examined in consultation and hospitalization at Brazzaville university teaching hospital. It confirms that ankylosing spondylitis is a rare disease in sub-Saharan black Africa.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
